# .gitignore = files and folders Git must NEVER save or upload.
# One pattern per line. "folder/" = a whole folder; "*.log" = every file ending in .log.

### SECRETS (never commit these) ###
# The real settings file holds the MySQL password. GitHub gets application.example.properties instead.
backend/src/main/resources/application.properties
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

### EVIDENCE (private data: images can contain GPS locations) ###
backend/uploads/

### LOGS ###
*.log

### BUILD OUTPUT (rebuilt automatically) ###
backend/target/
out/
frontend/dist/

### DOWNLOADED LIBRARIES (rebuilt from pom.xml / package.json / requirements.txt) ###
node_modules/
ai-service/.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

### IDE / OS files (personal to each computer) ###
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

### Leftovers from the IntelliJ "new project" template, not part of Truvira ###
/src/
/package-lock.json
